<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech Jan-April trade deficit CZK 53.65 bln.</title>
<headline>Czech Jan-April trade deficit CZK 53.65 bln.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-05-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Czech Republic posted a January-April trade deficit of 53.652 billion crowns, compared to a 39.644 billion crown deficit for the same period in 1996, the Czech Statistical Bureau (CSU) said on Monday.</p>
<p>The CSU figures showed that April's trade deficit was 15.334 billion crowns and that the March deficit was revised to 13.082 billion crowns from a previously reported 13.429 billion.  </p>
<p> CZECH FOREIGN TRADE  JAN-APRIL 97  JAN-MARCH 97   JAN-APRIL 96</p>
<p>  imports (CZK bln)     261.652    186.618 (188.199)  235.348</p>
<p>  exports		   208.000    148.299 (148.018)  195.704</p>
<p>  balance		   -53.652    -38.319 (-40.181)  -39.644</p>
<p>Note. All figures in billions of crowns on customs-cleared basis and subject to revision. Previously reported first quarter figures in brackets.  </p>
